  "reason": "For a d³ octahedral ion, the three lowest excited terms are the quartet states ⁴T₂g, ⁴T₁g(F), and ⁴T₁g(P); ⁴T₂g has E/B = 10(Dq/B), while the two ⁴T₁g states arise from configuration interaction between ⁴T₁g(F) and ⁴T₁g(P) and are obtained by solving the secular equation with matrix elements 18Dq, 15B+18Dq, and 2Dq coupling, giving energies that increase with Dq/B while maintaining the ordering ⁴T₂g < ⁴T₁g(F) < ⁴T₁g(P) across the range studied."
